WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.375
Which cloud matters here in three ways.

2
00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:06.755
The endpoints differ: servers in
Azure Government reach a government

3
00:00:06.755 --> 00:00:11.437
machine configuration host, with regional
endpoints in the US Gov regions.

4
00:00:11.437 --> 00:00:14.032
The way machines read the package matters:

5
00:00:14.032 --> 00:00:17.072
the build uses each machine's
own system identity,

6
00:00:17.072 --> 00:00:22.038
because Learn says a user-assigned identity
doesn't work for Arc-enabled servers.

7
00:00:22.038 --> 00:00:27.185
And cost: for Arc-enabled Windows servers
with the right licensing, it's included,

8
00:00:27.185 --> 00:00:31.084
but that activation isn't offered
in two of the US Gov regions,

9
00:00:31.084 --> 00:00:32.488
so plan to buy it there.

10
00:00:32.488 --> 00:00:35.540
This estate's servers
report to commercial Azure.
